{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1111836-character-creation-avoiding-common-pitfalls-as-a-new-player","id":1111836,"title":"Character Creation: avoiding common pitfalls as a new player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-05T15:23:49-07:00","id":1111836,"title":"Character Creation: avoiding common pitfalls as a new player","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I am a long-time Mage player (both oWoD and nWoD), with a minor amount of experience with Werewolf (primarily nWoD) and Vampire (a bit of oWoD but mostly nWoD). We might be transitioning to a Changeling game for a while (likely using the 2nd edition book and possibly other resources unless C20 hits relatively soon). I wanted to reach out about important considerations for creating Changeling characters from a mechanical perspective, with a focus on key things to avoid (especially if they might seem like decent ideas at first glance). To guide discussion, I will give a Mage example:<br /> <br /> The saying goes that a Mage character does not have an Arete (main power stat) of 1 and 15 freebie points to spend at character creation; they have an Arete of 3 and 7 freebie points. Because Mages (especially traditionalist Mages, the default PCs) often only roll their power stat to accomplish effects, rolling one die is a pretty terrible idea (botching and paradox galore). Also, one's Arete gates (limits) the amount one can have spheres at. An Arete of 1 would mean a character would have to place their 6 (that seems like a lot to many non-Mage players) sphere dots into six different spheres at only level 1 (which mostly involves powers of perception). At the very least, most (not all, but almost all) Mages should have an Arete of at least 2 (to enable 2-dot sphere choices and ability to influence things), if not an Arete of 3 (enabling one or possibly two 3-dot spheres at character creation if desired and a decent dice pool to actually do one of the main aspects of the game).<br /> <br /> So with that long-winded explanation, what pitfalls should I avoid in character creation? I am very attuned to focusing on concept, am reading the books to understand the setting, theme, and mood of the game, and am working with an ST who really knows this game and setting. I don't see issues there. I guess ultimately I have three topics/questions:<br /> <br /> 1) What I see are potential issues such as getting a few sessions into the game and realizing that my chosen realms do not align well with my chosen arts. Any insight into what aligns well or what not to overlook (e.g., needing Fae 2 to affect Sidhe?)<br /> <br /> 2) What are really wise places to spend freebie points? I likely will sit down and crunch out freebie point vs. experience point efficiency, but I know full well that's not the full picture (e.g., Backgrounds that aren't feasible to acquire after character creation, or more importantly for me, aspects specific to Changeling that are worth improving at character creation even if not the most efficient use of points). For Mages, the cost of willpower in terms of freebie points to experience points is kind of a no-brainer (Mages start with a default of 5, so pumping it up higher and higher just gets more efficient and is really helpful with actually pulling off magickal effects).<br /> <br /> I also need to keep in mind that we might not play this game for a super long time, so something that is efficient over a long period of time but handicaps a starting character might not be a great idea. And of course, all of this is much less about mechanical exploitation and much more about avoiding handicapping a character concept.<br /> <br /> 3) Are there any fairly important kiths or Arts (or Realms?) in books outside of the second edition core book? I have heard Kyros mentioned as an example.<br /> <br /> Thank you all, and apologies if there is a thread covering this already! I welcome any link to such a thread instead of folks feeling the need to repeat themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:56:15-07:00","id":1111911,"title":"","content":"Kenning and Gremayre are very important. They reflect fae senses (kenning) and comprehension of magic (gremayre).<br /> <br /> Arts and Realms- For a beginning character, its a good idea to choose a single Art. Realms allow versatility in that single Art. So if you hant magical skill, get those Realms up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T21:34:18-07:00","id":1111974,"title":"","content":"The Realms. Well you should always take at least enough Fae to affect yourself, one is enough if your a Commoner and two if your a Sidhe, and then Prop is a rather useful general Realm as you can use it to circumvent your limitations when it comes to affecting anything non-Fae. This is due to Actor realm limiting you to mostly dear friends while even one dot in Prop allows you to attack them by using nearby objects, or even their own clothing.<br /> <br /> Glamour is something you should consider as well since, especially if using 2nd edition, everything from most birthrights, cantrips, enchantment and generally doing anything at all tends to cost Glamour. If using C20 some of the costs have been adjusted, when it comes to birthrights, but you can use Glamour to boost your realms, and so magic, and you use your Glamour rating as dicepool to resist gaining Banality as well as resisting effects of the Mists, as they will start to affect you if having higher Banality than Glamour. Also as C20 allows you to Unleash your Arts using your Glamour as a dicepool I would nearly always consider buying it up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:08:43-07:00","id":1112054,"title":"","content":"What they said. I'd use the Mage costs for Willpower (one freebie per dot), for parity. Kryos is far from essential. Stick to the core Arts. C20 allows you to use Realms you don't have for an additional point of Glamour. I think you should probably steal that rule and, if you can, Google the preview of the Unleashing system that was released during the KS, as that will allow you to see if it's something you can use.<br /> <br /> If you're using Dragon's Ire, stock up on Remembrance.<br /> <br /> As for Glamour itself, C20 gives each kith a unique way to gain Glamour which is in-keeping with its nature, called Revelry. That would probably help with the scarcity of Glamour. Alternatively, increase the Glamour reaped from a freehold or let players get hold of lots of dross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:20:11-07:00","id":1112144,"title":"","content":"These are all really, really helpful responses. Thank you so much! I am hoping the timing works out so we can get C20 in our hands before starting play. I will google around for any helpful C20 previews, including any specifically mentioned here. Thank again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:51:50-07:00","id":1112552,"title":"","content":"I take any Art, that has max opportunities to buffs/debuffs + Fae 5, which allows me to affect me, companions, changelings, chimerae, fae and Cantrips ifself. Pretty good deal and aligns with my interests in game fiction. Just have to make sure, someone in the party prioritized in actors, props, nature and catch-all.<br /> <br /> I also try to take as much of Flaws/Advs to maximize Dreaming's particular brand of WEIRD. Because ingame means to acquire them only limited to Bedlam and chimera-crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:02:58-07:00","id":1112602,"title":"","content":"Regeneration is a good Merit, given fae squishiness. However, CTD2e is vague enough about damage that you could rule that changelings can soak all kinds of damage. C20 does away with that, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:04:34-07:00","id":1114741,"title":"","content":"Ah, so I imagine that C20 does not permit soaking lethal without armor or some other supernatural ability (or perhaps some kithain, such as Trolls, can soak lethal)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T06:37:14-07:00","id":1115065,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, changelings can soak only chimerical lethal normally, but may soak both chimerical and mundane lethal after calling upon the wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:22:41-07:00","id":1115348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1111836-character-creation-avoiding-common-pitfalls-as-a-new-player?p=1111911#post1111911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kenning and Gremayre are very important. They reflect fae senses (kenning) and comprehension of magic (gremayre).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd disagree with this. While these Abilities can be important for some characters, they haven't been a major point in most of my games. If it makes sense for the character, buy them up. For the average changeling you probably don't need to put more than a dot or two in each at the most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1111836-character-creation-avoiding-common-pitfalls-as-a-new-player?p=1111911#post1111911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arts and Realms- For a beginning character, its a good idea to choose a single Art. Realms allow versatility in that single Art. So if you hant magical skill, get those Realms up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'd respectfully disagree. If you want to be a fairly one-trick-pony then of course buy up a single Art. But if you want more diversity in what your cantrips can do, you'll want to divide your points into 2 or 3 of them, even if you aren't high level in any of them at the start. <br /> <br /> I really like the C20 description of Realms. It solves a big problem I had with previous editions, where you were pretty screwed if you didn't have a Realm high enough. For example, if you didn't have Actor 5 you couldn't directly affect a mortal enemy at all! That's pretty bad when that gangster or psychologist was dead set on taking you down. The new system has some penalties if you don't have the appropriate level, but you essentially have access to all levels. This means that when creating a character it's not quite as important to plunk a lot of points into Realms right off the bat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T04:30:12-07:00","id":1115466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1111836-character-creation-avoiding-common-pitfalls-as-a-new-player?p=1115348#post1115348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd disagree with this. While these Abilities can be important for some characters, they haven't been a major point in most of my games. If it makes sense for the character, buy them up. For the average changeling you probably don't need to put more than a dot or two in each at the most.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd respectfully disagree. If you want to be a fairly one-trick-pony then of course buy up a single Art. But if you want more diversity in what your cantrips can do, you'll want to divide your points into 2 or 3 of them, even if you aren't high level in any of them at the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I see your points.<br /> <br /> The guy starting is new to Changeling, so I figure keeping it simple but versatile is the way. I have seen a number of new players overstretch Arts, and then not have enough of a dice pool or the right Realms to do what they want. <br /> <br /> I am looking forward to seeing how C20 balances. Cantrips seem more potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-13-2017, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T07:08:23-07:00","id":1115514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1111836-character-creation-avoiding-common-pitfalls-as-a-new-player?p=1115348#post1115348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with previous editions, where you were pretty screwed if you didn't have a Realm high enough. For example, if you didn't have Actor 5 you couldn't directly affect a mortal enemy at all! That's pretty bad when that gangster or psychologist was dead set on taking you down.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly why, in previous editions especially (though useful still in C20 aswell), I always advocated players to take Prop as even though you couldn't affect the mortal, or prodigal, enemy you could just target his/her gun, clothes, car or just something else closeby that could be used against them with creative cantrips. Similarly that is why Fae is also a must so that you can affect yourself though sometimes that simply is not enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T17:44:13-07:00","id":1115728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1111836-character-creation-avoiding-common-pitfalls-as-a-new-player?p=1115466#post1115466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The guy starting is new to Changeling, so I figure keeping it simple but versatile is the way. I have seen a number of new players overstretch Arts, and then not have enough of a dice pool or the right Realms to do what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. I think it may come down to a person's preferred style of play. In a situation like this you can be really good at one thing or so-so at a few different things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:52:06-07:00","id":1118757,"title":"","content":"Fae 5 is super useful. In theory, manipulating Glamour itself can be interpreted broadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}